rselves for it and it's proper  sunscreen as well it's not  uh factor five factor 10 as i perhaps  used to wear in the in the 80s it's uh  it's proper 30 and 50 sunblock that  we're looking for absolutely and also  it's not just um older people who are  vulnerable because that's the  misconception that i think a lot of us  have but it looks as though from what  we're hearing that anybody really can be  at risk  anybody can be uh at risk at all we are  particularly concerned about people  living on their own uh and and older  people as well but um  anybody can be at this risk and it's not  something to be underestimated the  country uh doesn't see temperatures at  this kind of level and they bring uh  increased risk of mortality when they  when temperatures get this  and what are the signs to look out for  if somebody's struggling for example if  they're struggling with a heat stroke  for example how do you know that this is  what's happening to them  the important thing i think is to to ask  for advice if you are concerned about  people and if you are worried about it  then then one one one will give you uh  good advice so so don't um  you know exercise real caution and and  be really sensible about it and take  good early advice  on it if you are concerned

